      "question": "What does copyright enable creators to decide?",
      "http_status": 200,
      "elapsed_ms": 1605.234800001199,
      "answerable": true,
      "answer": "Copyright enables creators to decide who can share and reuse their creations.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "E001",
          "video_id": "64aa17cc-6ac4-44ab-b01a-43e2a3e179d7",
          "start_seconds": 0.0,
          "end_seconds": 42.4,
          "text": "Have you ever wondered how to download and share digital content legally? How do you let people know that you want them to reuse your own work? Creative Commons licenses can help you do both. We'll show you how. Our world's exploded with digital opportunities. Now we can communicate, share, and work together using the exceptional distribution network that is the internet. Information and content can fly between us in exciting new ways. But it's important to know that when something is created, say a photo or document or a music track, it's automatically protected by copyright. Copyright enables people to say who can share and reuse their creations.",
          "segment_ids": [
