          "video_id": "64aa17cc-6ac4-44ab-b01a-43e2a3e179d7",
          "start_seconds": 37.6,
          "end_seconds": 76.5,
          "text": "Copyright enables people to say who can share and reuse their creations. You must always obtain someone's permission before sharing or reusing their work, even when it's posted online. But what if a creator wants everyone to use their work without the hassle of granting permission over and over? This is where creative Commons can help. Creative Commons provides licensing tools that are free to use. You can apply a license to your work, which refines your copyright and streamlines how you give permission. Zach here downloads a photo called CC Kiwi that he wants to use in his science project.",
